# Loaded ONLY by `npm run build:android` (vite build --mode android).
# The normal web build (`npm run build`) never reads this file, so browser
# behaviour is unchanged.
#
# This is the public HTTPS URL of the hosted Karishma backend -- the same
# Express server from server.ts, deployed to Render by render.yaml. The web app
# and the APK therefore talk to ONE backend; nothing is duplicated.
#
# IMPORTANT: Render derives the hostname from the service name in render.yaml
# (`karishma-ai`). If that name was already taken in your Render workspace,
# Render appends a suffix -- open the service in the dashboard, copy the real
# URL shown at the top, and replace the value below before building the APK.
#
# No trailing slash.
#
# src/lib/native.ts reads this at build time and rewrites every relative
# `fetch("/api/...")` onto it, but ONLY when running inside the Capacitor
# WebView. To repoint an already-installed APK without rebuilding, run this
# from chrome://inspect:
#   localStorage.setItem("karishma_api_base", "https://your-backend")
#
# Only PUBLIC values belong in this file: it is compiled into the APK, which is
# a redistributable zip that anyone can unpack. No OpenRouter key, no Supabase
# service-role key, no Brevo key -- those stay as Render environment variables
# and are only ever read by server.ts.
VITE_API_BASE=https://karishma-ai.onrender.com
